"""
train_airbus_unet_crop_curriculum_hades.py

Airbus Ship Detection (Kaggle) — HADES environment
U-Net binary segmentation with:
- Mixture-of-Crops (POS ship-centered / NEG ship-free / CONTEXT)
- Curriculum over epochs (Phase1 fixed-size -> Phase2 multi-scale -> Phase3 distribution return)
- FP32 only (NO AMP)
- Single GPU / single process (NO DDP)
- Robust handling for corrupted images
- End-to-end: split -> train -> val threshold tune -> (optional) infer test_v2 -> submission.csv
- Optional Grad-CAM visualization (original + pred overlay + grad-cam overlay concat JPEG)

Embedding loss:
- NOT applied in this version (as requested).
- Scaffolding hooks are left so you can add embedding head/loss later without rewriting everything.

Dependencies:
- torch, torchvision, numpy, pillow
- Optional: opencv-python(-headless) OR scipy (for connected components / morphology)

Notes:
- IMPORTANT: ALL_TRAIN_IDS must be built from train_v2 directory (CSV contains only positives).
- Mask resize uses NEAREST.
- Image resize uses BILINEAR.

Authoring constraints from user:
- HADES paths under /workspace
- Copy-paste runnable, no omissions
"""

